# What git holds here is the SOURCE OF TRUTH, not the output.
#
# The pipeline is built so that descriptors, prompts and specs are the authored
# artifacts and the media is a function of them: BUILD-SPEC §2b rule 5 makes every
# generation content-addressed, so an identical prompt+model+params reuses the cached
# object instead of regenerating. That means a render is reproducible from what is
# committed here, and a 174MB tree of PNGs is a cache, not a deliverable. Media belongs
# in object storage (B2), keyed by hash, with the descriptor in git pointing at it.
#
# The rule of thumb: if a tool wrote it, it is ignored. If a person or a model was
# *asked* to write it and the answer was kept, it is committed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
# AGENT_GCP_KEY / GCP_PROJECT live here. Never commit; see .env.example.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- environments
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- caches
# .cache/ is the content-addressed store generate_stills.py writes through. Deleting it
# costs money to refill, which is exactly why it is a cache and not a source.
.cache/
content/.cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- generated media
# Renders, stills and takes. All reproducible from the YAML that is committed.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.MOV
*.mp3
*.wav
*.m4a
*.webm

# Generated stills (768x1344 PNGs, ~1.3MB each). The prompt that made each one is in
# the edit, and its sidecar records model + hash, so the picture itself is derivable.
*.png

# KEPT DELIBERATELY: the brand thumbnail. It is a build output like the stills above, but
# the rule there is "derivable, so drop it" and this one is not — GitHub's social preview,
# Devpost and anyone embedding the README need the raster itself, and re-rendering it
# needs librsvg plus Futura installed. Source of truth is still the SVG beside it.
!docs/brand/*.png

# KEPT DELIBERATELY: the console showcase. The rule above is "derivable, so drop it", and
# these are not: docs/showcase/capture.py rebuilds them only against a running instance
# that still holds the records it shoots — a measured song, a consented artist, five
# delivered kits — and that data is gitignored dev state, not something the repo carries.
# 8.6MB for fifteen screens, and they are the only picture of the console anyone gets
# without checking it out and running it.
!docs/showcase/*.png

# Camera-original photography — large, and not what this repo is for.
*.heic
*.HEIC

# KEPT DELIBERATELY: *.jpg. These are the hook reference frames the style anchor is
# built from (characters/*-ref*.jpg). They are small, and they are the only record of
# what the image model was actually shown — losing them makes a rerun unreproducible.

# KEPT DELIBERATELY: the demo overlay set. The *.png rule above is aimed at 1.3MB stills
# off an image model; these are 40KB of vector drawing each, 3MB for all twenty, and they
# are the deliverable for the demo edit rather than an intermediate on the way to one.
# Same call already made for the rendered PDFs in docs/. The ProRes masters are *not*
# kept — 33MB a card, and `generate_overlays.py --formats mov` rebuilds them.
!content/videos/demo-founder/*.png
!content/videos/demo-founder/*.webm

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- vendored binaries
# 38MB standalone; fetch it rather than carry it.
content/bin/yt-dlp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- agent worktrees
# `git worktree add` puts a checkout here, and a checkout inside a checkout is a repo
# inside a repo: `git add .` at the root stages it as a gitlink to a commit no clone can
# resolve, and the outer repo then carries a submodule nobody declared. Ignored rather
# than remembered — the failure is silent at `add` time and confusing forever after.
#
# Only `worktrees/`, not all of `.claude/`: settings, skills and agent definitions under
# it are authored files and belong in git by the rule at the top of this file.
.claude/worktrees/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- os noise
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db

# Diagram build intermediates (infra/architecture.pdf is the committed deliverable).
infra/.build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- app
app/.venv/
app/.remixkit-data/
app/**/__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- terraform
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform.lock.hcl
terraform.tfvars

# Built on demand for sharing; the served page is index.html + wireframe.json
docs/wireframe/standalone.html
